&gt;&gt; President Crave and members of the

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:35.840 align:start position:19%
committee of the whole. For the record,
I'm Mayor Patrick Collins. The six penny

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:39.680 align:start position:19%
sales tax has had an amazing impact on
our community over the years. It's the

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:44.720 align:start position:19%
only funding mechanism we have to
complete large infrastructure, quality

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:49.440 align:start position:19%
of life, and public safety projects.
Today, we have new fire stations, an

00:02:46.879 --> 00:02:54.480 align:start position:19%
active pavement management program, and
almost 50 miles of greenway system, a

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:57.680 align:start position:19%
developing downtown, and so much more
because of the investments that have

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:03.360 align:start position:19%
been made possible by the six penny
sales tax. The voters of Larry County

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:08.319 align:start position:19%
have been so awesome and so supportive.
The challenge for this ballot is that we

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:12.000 align:start position:19%
have more requests than projects than
the excuse me the Larmy County

00:03:10.159 --> 00:03:18.480 align:start position:19%
commissioners have granted to the city.
We were allocated $74,250,000

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:23.680 align:start position:19%
and the original request we had was in
excess of $150 million. The election is

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:28.319 align:start position:19%
scheduled for August 18th, the date of
the primary election with early voting

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:32.400 align:start position:19%
starting July 2nd.
The C county commissioners have

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:36.239 align:start position:19%
scheduled the first meeting of the
countywide committee made up of two

00:03:34.319 --> 00:03:40.799 align:start position:19%
members each from Pine Bluffs, Burns,
Alban, the county commission, and city

00:03:38.239 --> 00:03:44.319 align:start position:19%
of Cheyenne for next Wednesday. They
will begin the work of putting together

00:03:42.159 --> 00:03:48.080 align:start position:19%
the ballot that we will put forward next
summer. To give the governing body a

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:52.720 align:start position:19%
place to start, I have prepared a
resolution to start the discussion. And

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:56.959 align:start position:19%
here are some of my priorities.
5 years ago, we had aging fire stations

00:03:55.040 --> 00:04:01.840 align:start position:19%
that were not placed in the optimal
positions due to growth of the city. In

00:03:59.519 --> 00:04:04.799 align:start position:19%
the last six penny sales tax, the voters
approved building three new fire

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:09.680 align:start position:19%
stations that have helped improve
response times in our community safety.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:13.760 align:start position:19%
One area that still has response time
challenges is South Cheyenne. The

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:18.000 align:start position:19%
growing sweetgrass, Harmony, and Meta
areas are in need of improved response

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:22.079 align:start position:19%
times by our fire department. That could
be accomplished by moving station two,

00:04:19.919 --> 00:04:26.240 align:start position:19%
currently on Fox Farm Road to the land
the city's already purchased near the

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:30.800 align:start position:19%
corner of College Drive and South Griley
Highway. It will cover the growing areas

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:36.320 align:start position:19%
in the south and maximize the area that
two company can service. The request for

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:40.000 align:start position:19%
this is $12 million.
Again, 5 years ago, our fire

00:04:37.759 --> 00:04:44.240 align:start position:19%
department's apparatuses were aging and
struggling with reliability. We decided

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:48.720 align:start position:19%
that a vehicle replacement plan was
needed to keep our mainline fire engines

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:53.360 align:start position:19%
current and functioning. We purchased
four engines at that time and we need to

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:59.120 align:start position:19%
replace three more with this ballot. You
can see our current vehicles that we're

00:04:54.800 --> 00:05:02.800 align:start position:19%
using are 2008, 1998, and 2001. With the
lead time to order new fire engines at

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:07.120 align:start position:19%
four years, it makes managing our fleet
more challenging. But we hope to

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:11.160 align:start position:19%
purchase two fire engines and a ladder
truck at a cost of 5,23,364.

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:21.199 align:start position:19%
Cheyenne has a 370 mile road system
valued at close to a billion. For the

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:25.759 align:start position:19%
past years, we've engaged in a robust
pavement management program to stabilize

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:29.280 align:start position:19%
the condition of our roadways. Our city
engineer has calculated it will take at

00:05:27.199 --> 00:05:33.680 align:start position:19%
least $10 million a year just to
stabilize our roads. The fifth penny

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:37.440 align:start position:19%
contributes just over 5 million to our
pavement management program, leaving a

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:43.039 align:start position:19%
deficit that we must make up if we want
to continue improving our roadways. I've

00:05:40.479 --> 00:05:46.800 align:start position:19%
included $9 million in this request.
This amount is not the full request made

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:50.639 align:start position:19%
by our engineer. I've asked that he use
fifth penny sales tax overages that will

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:54.080 align:start position:19%
become available next year to make up
the difference. Maintaining our roads is

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:58.479 align:start position:19%
one of the highest priorities of our
residents and I hope you will maintain

00:05:55.759 --> 00:06:02.800 align:start position:19%
this level of funding going, keep this
level of funding going. um so that we

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:06.720 align:start position:19%
can keep our management program moving
forward. It's more cost-effective to

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:09.919 align:start position:19%
maintain roads than it is to replace
them.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:13.759 align:start position:19%
Our police department is asking for
technology to improve their operations.

00:06:12.319 --> 00:06:17.039 align:start position:19%
Incar cameras have reached the end of
their lives. There's newer, better

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:20.800 align:start position:19%
technology, and replacing them is one of
their highest priorities. AI is also a

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:24.880 align:start position:19%
tool that makes a difference in law
enforcement and Chief Francisco is

00:06:22.639 --> 00:06:29.120 align:start position:19%
asking for funding to purchase AI tools
to help with the efficiency of the

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:33.440 align:start position:19%
department. This $3,700,000
request includes a 5-year digital

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:38.319 align:start position:19%
storage plan, and I believe technology
can be a force multiplier for our or

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:42.560 align:start position:19%
excuse me, our police department.
Chief Dyorn is asking for some essential

00:06:40.319 --> 00:06:46.800 align:start position:19%
equipment that he can't pay for with his
fifth penny sales tax allocation. The

00:06:45.199 --> 00:06:50.400 align:start position:19%
fire department issues personal
protective gear to each firefighter.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:54.000 align:start position:19%
This turnout gear is scheduled to be
replaced as it will reach its end of

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:59.080 align:start position:19%
life during the next couple of years.
And we know 90 sets of the gear will

00:06:55.759 --> 00:06:59.080 align:start position:19%
cost $459,340.

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:05.919 align:start position:19%
The chief is also asking for funding to
replace 50 portable radios that will

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:09.240 align:start position:19%
also reach their end of life at a cost
of $599,947.

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:18.639 align:start position:19%
The Greenway is one of the gems of our
city. Starting in 1991, we have used the

00:07:16.639 --> 00:07:24.080 align:start position:19%
six penny sales tax to make incremental
additions over the past 35 years. I

00:07:21.759 --> 00:07:28.639 align:start position:19%
think we're just under 50 miles now of
paved greenway. Because we have greenway

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:33.120 align:start position:19%
infrastructure reaching about 35 years
old, dedicated funding for maintenance

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:37.759 align:start position:19%
is critical. The total request for the
greenway is $6 million split between

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:40.720 align:start position:19%
maintenance
and funding the incremental additions

00:07:39.199 --> 00:07:44.639 align:start position:19%
that we will hope will keep the greenway
system growing.

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:49.520 align:start position:19%
In our last six penny sales tax
approval, the voters funded $6 million

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:52.880 align:start position:19%
to make improvements to our downtown. It
has made such a difference and I don't

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:57.280 align:start position:19%
want to lose the momentum that we made
over the past four years. Investing an

00:07:55.120 --> 00:08:02.319 align:start position:19%
additional $4 million in our downtown
will continue to make it a destination

00:07:59.199 --> 00:08:07.039 align:start position:19%
for tourism and a focal point for our
residents.

00:08:04.639 --> 00:08:11.280 align:start position:19%
Our police department trains with their
weapons every month. The current shoot

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:14.800 align:start position:19%
house is falling apart and does not have
the capability to move walls to create

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:17.919 align:start position:19%
the different scenarios the trainers
would like to have. The police

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:21.840 align:start position:19%
department is asking for a million
dollars to build a new show house shoot

00:08:19.919 --> 00:08:26.319 align:start position:19%
house with the flexibility to move the
walls and to improve their outdoor

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:29.199 align:start position:19%
firing line. This kind of training is
essential to prevent the unthinkable

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:33.599 align:start position:19%
events we see happening across the
country every year.

00:08:31.919 --> 00:08:37.360 align:start position:19%
The largest request is to completely
remodel the municipal building we're

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:42.719 align:start position:19%
sitting in. It was completed in the late
1970s and the essential HVAC, electrical

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:46.320 align:start position:19%
and plumbing systems have started to
reach the end of their useful lives and

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:50.880 align:start position:19%
they now present operational safety and
reliability concerns I don't believe we

00:08:48.399 --> 00:08:54.480 align:start position:19%
can further defer.
We've had to close this building what

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:58.800 align:start position:19%
two or three times now in the last few
years uh due to these kind of failures.

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:03.440 align:start position:19%
Additionally, the current current
configuration no longer supports the

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:07.279 align:start position:19%
needs of our operation. We used the $2.5
million approved by the voters on the

00:09:05.279 --> 00:09:12.640 align:start position:19%
last six penny sales tax election to
start that plan for the remodel and $22

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:16.320 align:start position:19%
million is the request for this effort.
I believe we owe it to our employees to

00:09:14.399 --> 00:09:19.920 align:start position:19%
give this building attention and moving
all the public-f facing municipal

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:26.160 align:start position:19%
services to the first floor will make a
big improvement in our customer service.

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:30.880 align:start position:19%
Johnson pool. Now, that's an amenity
that people have loved for many years,

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:34.720 align:start position:19%
but after 71 years, it's finally reached
the end of its life. We spent the

00:09:32.959 --> 00:09:39.360 align:start position:19%
funding approved on the last six penny
sales tax selection for the design to

00:09:37.279 --> 00:09:42.800 align:start position:19%
replace the pool. By choosing the
outdoor option, we'll save money on the

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:48.080 align:start position:19%
construction and the ongoing operation
costs. 10,400,000

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:52.720 align:start position:19%
is the cost to build this new Johnson
outdoor pool.

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:57.279 align:start position:19%
Unfortunately, many very worthy projects
did make my list uh of priorities. U and

00:09:56.080 --> 00:10:01.440 align:start position:19%
I'd like to just go through those real
quickly. Fire station 6 replacement did

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:05.600 align:start position:19%
