asked the staff to conserve these funds

00:10:10.959 --> 00:10:18.240 align:start position:19%
so we can focus on building fire station
6 in the future and we currently have $2

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:23.279 align:start position:19%
million towards that effort.
Reed Avenue was approved in 2017 and we

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:27.440 align:start position:19%
spent the last 5 years trying to gain
railroad approval to do the project.

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:31.040 align:start position:19%
We've made great progress in gaining
their approval and I do believe we'll

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:34.800 align:start position:19%
eventually we'll be able to sign an
agreement with the Burlington Northern

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:39.600 align:start position:19%
Railroad. We've been told it will take
at least 18 months to get there. I

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:42.640 align:start position:19%
believe it would be irresponsible to put
funding for a project on the ballot

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:48.160 align:start position:19%
where we don't own the property and we
don't have permission to construct.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:51.279 align:start position:19%
Engineer Cobb has shared with me that he
believes that we can build the Reed

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:55.600 align:start position:19%
Avenue project for much much less than
the $14 million estimated by the

00:10:53.440 --> 00:11:00.240 align:start position:19%
consultants.
I propose that we save the remaining

00:10:57.279 --> 00:11:04.880 align:start position:19%
funds left from the 2017 ballot, use it
as a match for a grant request to the

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:09.600 align:start position:19%
state, and maybe use a little bit of our
general fund reserves to construct the

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:12.560 align:start position:19%
project. We have gained those approvals.
Engineer Cobb is working on the

00:11:10.959 --> 00:11:16.079 align:start position:19%
estimates, but we think we can build it
for maybe about a third or just slightly

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:20.560 align:start position:19%
over a third of what that engineer
estimate is.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:24.399 align:start position:19%
The pump house is another project that
didn't make the list, but it's been on

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:28.480 align:start position:19%
our agenda a lot recently. After we
voted to remove the demolition deadline,

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:31.600 align:start position:19%
Director Sanchez came to me with an idea
to make the pump house the new

00:11:30.079 --> 00:11:34.640 align:start position:19%
headquarters for the Clean and Safe
project.

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:39.600 align:start position:19%
We've been looking for a couple years,
Jason and I have in our downtown for a

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:44.240 align:start position:19%
warehouse and a place for the clean and
safe, but nothing has become available.

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:48.079 align:start position:19%
This is a project that I think we should
pay for with general fund reserves. We

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:52.560 align:start position:19%
have an estimate around $3 million and
we're working to get that finalized, but

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:58.320 align:start position:19%
we would solve two problems. We would
save the pump house and we'd find a home

00:11:55.279 --> 00:12:01.440 align:start position:19%
for the clean and safe program.
Five years ago, I was concerned that we

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:06.800 align:start position:19%
might not be in a position to afford the
minimum revenue guarantees to

00:12:04.399 --> 00:12:12.480 align:start position:19%
required uh to maintain our passenger
air service at the airport. Our budget

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:16.639 align:start position:19%
feature at that time was not
it was a concern.

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:21.760 align:start position:19%
The voters approved the MRG request and
at the end of November, we still had

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:25.279 align:start position:19%
1.25 million left in that account. I
feel that commercial passenger service

00:12:23.839 --> 00:12:29.680 align:start position:19%
is a very high priority for the
community, but I didn't rank it high

00:12:27.279 --> 00:12:34.480 align:start position:19%
enough to make the ballot is I believe
with the $1.25 million left, we'll be

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:38.480 align:start position:19%
able to use our budget, which I think is
growing, to be able to fund the MRG

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:42.720 align:start position:19%
until the end of the next six penny
sales tax.

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:46.480 align:start position:19%
Another project that um I fully support
is the old airport terminal. And I'm

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:52.160 align:start position:19%
really excited about that project.
Bringing a res restaurant, a museum, an

00:12:48.959 --> 00:12:56.959 align:start position:19%
art center to the uh site at the old uh
terminal would be amazing. I just didn't

00:12:54.880 --> 00:13:00.240 align:start position:19%
rank the $4 million project high enough
for it to make the ballot. But I do want

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:04.880 align:start position:19%
to work with the airport to find a way
to make this project happen.

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:08.720 align:start position:19%
But the police department asked for
$975,000

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:13.040 align:start position:19%
to purchase two multi-purpose rescue
vehicles to replace their current

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:17.360 align:start position:19%
military surplus vehicles. the new
vehicles would just fit better in an

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:20.959 align:start position:19%
urban law enforcement environment, but I
couldn't fit them onto the budget. But

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:24.000 align:start position:19%
now that we know exactly what they're
looking for, I believe that we'll be

00:13:22.399 --> 00:13:28.560 align:start position:19%
able to find alternative ways to pay for
that in the future. And lastly, the

00:13:26.399 --> 00:13:32.720 align:start position:19%
police department asked for $500,000 to
construct a multi-bay storage building

00:13:30.639 --> 00:13:36.720 align:start position:19%
to hold all their various equipment, do
it in one place, and I support this

00:13:34.959 --> 00:13:39.920 align:start position:19%
project and would recommend rather than
waiting for the sixth penny that we use

00:13:38.399 --> 00:13:44.320 align:start position:19%
general fund reserves and make it happen
right away. Mr. President, those are my

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:48.639 align:start position:19%
recommendations for the next six penny.
I look forward to our discussions and I

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:52.560 align:start position:19%
really look forward to uh selling and
educating the public uh and the Larmy

00:13:50.639 --> 00:13:55.279 align:start position:19%
County voters about these projects.
Thank you.

